## Understanding the code

| Syntax | Description |
|---|---|
| `+materialized: streaming_table` (in `dbt_project.yml`) | Every Bronze model becomes a Streaming Table. Each job run processes only newly arrived files. |
| `from stream read_files('/Volumes/...', format => ...)` | **Auto Loader**: discovers and reads new files in the landing Volume. {{ s.source.format_note }} |
| `{{ '{{' }} target.catalog {{ '}}' }}` | Resolves to the catalog you select in the dbt task, so the same project runs in every learner's catalog. |
| `_ingested_at`, `_source` | Audit columns that record when data was ingested and which file it came from (`_metadata.file_path`). |
{% for src in s.sources if src.kinesis %}

!!! tip "In production: read {{ src.name }} straight from Kinesis"
    In this lab, the {{ src.name }} events from Amazon Kinesis have already been landed as JSON files in the Volume. In production, the same Bronze model can read the stream directly with the `read_kinesis` streaming table function and a Unity Catalog service credential, then parse the payload:

    ```sql
    select
      from_json(cast(data as string), '{{ src.kinesis.schema_hint }}') as event,
      approximateArrivalTimestamp as _ingested_at,
      stream as _source
    from stream read_kinesis(
      streamName => '{{ src.kinesis.stream_name }}',
      initialPosition => 'trim_horizon',
      serviceCredential => '<service_credential_name>'
    )
    ```

    See [read_kinesis](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/sql/language-manual/functions/read_kinesis) for the options.
{% endfor %}

!!! tip "Role of the Bronze layer"
    The Bronze layer preserves source data **unchanged**. If cleansing logic changes later, you can reprocess from Bronze without re-ingesting the raw data.

